    <div class=3D"s-prose js-post-body" itemprop=3D"text">
<p>If you want to checkout just the files with valid paths, you can do (in =
Git Bash):</p>
<pre><code>git clone --sparse -c core.protectNTFS=3Dfalse -n &lt;repo-URL&g=
t;
git sparse-checkout add "\!&lt;pattern1&gt;" "\!&lt;pattern2&gt;"
git checkout &lt;branch&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Patterns are relative to repo root and can use <code>*</code></p>
<p>More info <a href=3D"https://github.com/git-for-windows/git/issues/2777"=
 rel=3D"noreferrer">here</a> and <a href=3D"https://github.com/git-for-wind=
ows/git/issues/2803" rel=3D"noreferrer">here</a>.</p>
<p>However if you actually need those files to e.g. build the project, my b=
est bet to do this on Windows would be to use <a href=3D"https://en.wikiped=
ia.org/wiki/Windows_Subsystem_for_Linux" rel=3D"noreferrer">WSL</a>.</p>
    </div>
