    <div class=3D"s-prose js-post-body" itemprop=3D"text">
<p>As @Wendy said, just install de WSL on Windows, you can use this link:
<a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/pt-br/windows/wsl/install" rel=3D"no=
follow noreferrer">https://learn.microsoft.com/pt-br/windows/wsl/install</a=
>
Btw I chose the Ubuntu.</p>
<p>In case you choose Ubuntu too, follow the next steps to install:</p>
<pre><code>wsl --install -d Ubuntu
</code></pre>
<p>When the Ubuntu terminal shows up:</p>
<pre><code>sudo apt update &amp;&amp; sudo apt upgrade
</code></pre>
<p>And after you need to install git on WSL and configure, fallow the next =
steps:</p>
<p><code>sudo apt-get install git</code></p>
<p>Then</p>
<pre><code>git config --global user.name "your_github_username"
git config --global user.email "your_github_email"
git config -l
</code></pre>
<p>You have to use a personal token to authenticate to your Git account, so=
 fallow this steps:
My Account =E2=86=92 Settings =E2=86=92 Developer settings =E2=86=92 Person=
al access tokens =E2=86=92 Generate new token</p>
<p>To clone your repo use:
<code>git clone https://&lt;tokenhere&gt;@github.com/&lt;user&gt;/&lt;repo&=
gt;.git</code></p>
<p>To find your files from WSL in Windows explorer you can use in the repo =
folder this command:</p>
<p><code>explorer.exe .</code></p>
